77
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:45,140
Now success fantasies, Gabriel Ottingen's research separates two things

78
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:45,960
that feel alike.

79
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:49,220
Positive expectations are a judgment that you are likely

80
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:49,980
to succeed.

81
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:54,420
Positive fantasies are vivid, pleasant images of the desired

82
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:54,960
future.

83
00:03:55,660 --> 00:03:58,760
Expectations predicted high effort and good results.

84
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:03,340
Fantasies predicted the reverse, less effort and worse results.

85
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:07,600
In one study, 83 German students rated their fantasies

86
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:10,020
about graduating and landing a job.

87
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:13,780
Two years later, those with the most positive fantasies

88
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:18,020
had sent fewer applications, received fewer offers, and earned

89
00:04:18,020 --> 00:04:18,880
lower salaries.

90
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:23,200
The same pattern held for romantic crushes, recovery from

91
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:25,160
hip surgery, and weight loss.

92
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:29,860
Experiments show how positive fantasy lowered systolic blood pressure,

93
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:33,600
a marker of physical energy, by 1 .73 points

94
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:35,960
while a fantasy raised it slightly.

95
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:39,620
Students who fantasized about an ideal week felt less

96
00:04:39,620 --> 00:04:42,220
energized right away and got less done a week

97
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:42,640
later.

98
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:46,900
In the researchers words positive fantasies let people mentally

99
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:50,400
consummate a desired future so effort feels unnecessary.

100
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:53,240
The drain was bigger when the need was more

101
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:53,620
pressing.

102
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,760
The mood effect also flips.

103
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:59,960
Positive fantasies went with fewer depressive symptoms at the

104
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:03,740
same moment but predicted more depressive symptoms up to

105
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:06,840
seven months later, partly through lower grades.

106
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:10,520
Fantasies also bias you toward looking at a goal's

107
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:14,300
upsides over its downsides, which leads to worse decisions.

108
00:05:15,060 --> 00:05:16,880
There is an evidence -based remedy.

109
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:21,960
Mental contrasting with implementation intentions, known as WOOP, pairs

110
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:24,060
